-- title:
--   Stalks of the two-chart integral model over a Noetherian base
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative Noetherian domain, let $F$ be a field equipped with an $R$-algebra structure whose structure map $R \to F$ is injective, and let $j \in F$ be an element assumed nonzero (as a `Fact` instance). For a subset $S \subseteq F$, `chartAlg R F S` is the $R$-subalgebra of $F$ consisting of those $x \in F$ that are integral over the subring $R[S]$ generated by $S$; write `chartAlgFin` $=$ `chartAlg R F {j}` and `chartAlgInf` $=$ `chartAlg R F {j⁻¹}`. Assume both are of finite type as $R$-algebras. Let $X =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel R F j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) be the pushout of schemes of the two morphisms `fFin R F j` and `fInf R F j` obtained by applying $\operatorname{Spec}$ to the inclusions of the two chart algebras into the middle ring, and let `toBase R F j` $: X \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ be the morphism descending the structure morphisms $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{chartAlgFin}) \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ and $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{chartAlgInf}) \to \operatorname{Spec} R$. Let $z$ be a point of $X$, and suppose the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ is given an $R$-algebra structure whose structure map sends $r \in R$ to the germ at $z$ of the pullback along `toBase R F j` of the global section of $\operatorname{Spec} R$ corresponding to $r$ under the inverse of `Scheme.ΓSpecIso`. Then $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ is a Noetherian ring, is essentially of finite type over $R$, is an integral domain, and the structure map $R \to \mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ is injective.
--
--   This records the basic local algebra of the two-chart integral model of a curve: each of its local rings is a Noetherian local domain, essentially of finite type and faithful over the Noetherian base $R$. It is used downstream when the model is compared with smooth or normal proper models over discrete valuation rings and in the construction of integral models of modular curves.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel_isNoetherianRing_stalk_and_essFiniteType_and_isDomain_and_injective.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

